{
  "_note": "Open-weight SPEECH models — STT (speech recognition) and TTS (speech synthesis). Distinct from data/speech.json, which is a static reference table of prices and rough VRAM; this file is the calculator dataset. Sizes marked source 'registry' were derived from the ACTUAL staged weights in ThakiCloud's s3://ai-platform/global/models registry (shard bytes / on-disk dtype); sizes marked 'card' come from the published model card. Speech has its own physics again: the unit of work is a SECOND OF AUDIO, not a token or a denoising step, so the headline number is the real-time factor (RTF) — how many seconds of audio you process per second of wall clock. Unlike diffusion, concurrency DOES help here (measured: Granite Speech 37.9x realtime at concurrency 1, 124x at concurrency 8 through vLLM), because these are ordinary transformer forward passes that batch well. `measured` rows are OUR OWN single-B200 runs; ASR accuracy is LibriSpeech clean-validation (64 utterances, 304s). Models we could not run are recorded as blocked with the reason, because 'no runtime exists' is the single most useful fact about a speech model and it is never on the model card.",
